#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:13
msgid "Plan Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:15
msgid "Use this skill when the user wants a plan instead of execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:17
msgid "Core behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:19
msgid "For this turn, you are planning only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:21
msgid "Do not implement code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:22
msgid "Do not edit project files except the plan markdown file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"Do not run mutating terminal commands, commit, push, or perform external "
"actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"You may inspect the repo or other context with read-only commands/tools "
"when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"Your deliverable is a markdown plan saved inside the active workspace "
"under `.hermes/plans/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:27
msgid "Output requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:29
msgid "Write a markdown plan that is concrete and actionable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:31
msgid "Include, when relevant:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:32
msgid "Goal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:33
msgid "Current context / assumptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:34
msgid "Proposed approach"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:35
msgid "Step-by-step plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:36
msgid "Files likely to change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:37
msgid "Tests / validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:38
msgid "Risks, tradeoffs, and open questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"If the task is code-related, include exact file paths, likely test "
"targets, and verification steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:42
msgid "Save location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:44
msgid "Save the plan with `write_file` under:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:45
msgid "`.hermes/plans/YYYY-MM-DD_HHMMSS-<slug>.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:47
msgid ""
"Treat that as relative to the active working directory / backend "
"workspace. Hermes file tools are backend-aware, so using this relative "
"path keeps the plan with the workspace on local, docker, ssh, modal, and "
"daytona backends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:49
msgid ""
"If the runtime provides a specific target path, use that exact path. If "
"not, create a sensible timestamped filename yourself under "
"`.hermes/plans/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:52
msgid "Interaction style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:54
msgid "If the request is clear enough, write the plan directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:55
msgid ""
"If no explicit instruction accompanies `/plan`, infer the task from the "
"current conversation context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:56
msgid ""
"If it is genuinely underspecified, ask a brief clarifying question "
"instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/plan_SKILL.md:57
msgid ""
"After saving the plan, reply briefly with what you planned and the saved "
"path."
msgstr ""

